<resources>
    <!--
      Error messages, one per reachable DataError constant.

      Each says what happened and, where the user can do something, what. None
      of them name a cause the user cannot act on, and none blame the user for a
      fault that is ours.

      Apostrophes are NOT escaped here. Compose Resources is not aapt: its
      Gradle plugin unescapes only \uXXXX, \n, \t and \\, and the runtime
      returns the text verbatim — so a \' would ship a visible backslash to the
      user. For the same reason, any future placeholder must be indexed
      (%1$s, %1$d); a bare %s is emitted literally with no error.
    -->
    <string name="error_no_internet">No internet connection. Check your connection and try again.</string>
    <string name="error_request_timeout">The request took too long. Try again.</string>
    <string name="error_not_found">We couldn't find what you were looking for.</string>
    <string name="error_too_many_requests">Too many requests. Wait a moment and try again.</string>
    <string name="error_server">The server is having trouble. Try again later.</string>
    <!-- Our bug, not theirs: the response arrived but did not match what we expected. -->
    <string name="error_serialization">We couldn't read the server's response.</string>
    <string name="error_disk_full">There's no space left on your device.</string>
    <!--
      Source-neutral on purpose: DataError.Local.UNKNOWN comes from reads
      (getFavorite, and the local-first getCharacter behind the detail screen) as
      well as writes, so it must not claim a save failed.
    -->
    <string name="error_local_unknown">Something went wrong on your device. Try again.</string>
    <string name="error_unknown">Something went wrong. Try again.</string>
</resources>
